sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task + full intent as inputs, single Swamp Node, DECISIONS 1 (token minted at admission, vault.get), Gateway renders .env from the Project env template (orbit-gateway-renders-create-env; Nick 2026-11-01), budget rule swamp-operation-time-budgets (<10 s, 60 s).
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 1-22 (rule 22: cfgmgmt file/systemd, 0600 credential file for the private fetch).
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: instance:create
  %% kind: instance.create
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: instance:create 7 12 blog<br/>--branch=… --domain=…
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:create 7 12 blog --branch=feature/blog`
  %%> - syntax: `<project> <node> <name> [--branch=BRANCH] [--domain=HOST] [--root=PATH] [--database-server=SLUG]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - Project, app-dev Node and Instance name
  %%> - optional: branch, domain, Database server for the Instance's database
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, render .env<br/>Instance 42 reserved, task #5121
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - the Node has the `app-dev` role
  %%> - the Project may be placed on this Node (not excluded)
  %%> - the Instance name and path are free
  %%> Renders .env:
  %%> - from the Project's stored env template, with its placeholders
  %%> - filled with Instance values: `APP_URL`, a new `APP_KEY`, database keys
  %%> Result:
  %%> - Instance 42 recorded as reserved, with its rendered environment
  %%> - task #5121 recorded with the full intent
  %%> - nothing has happened on the Node yet
  GW->>SW: Push token and .env<br/>vault: github-token, env-5121
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the repository is private, so the clone needs a GitHub token
  %%> - only the Gateway holds the GitHub App key
  %%> - `.env` can hold secrets, which travel only through the vault
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - mints a read token for this one repository, valid 1 hour
  %%> - pushes the token and the rendered `.env` into Swamp's vault
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the run reads both from the vault; no step calls the Gateway back (decision 1)
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-create · 60 s
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one run of `operation-instance-create` on Swamp serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - everything the run needs: Node address, paths, branch, setup steps
  %%> - secrets only as vault key names
  %%> Budget:
  %%> - 60 s for the whole run, target under 10 s
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>operation #5121
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the work continues in Swamp; the CLI follows it with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Clone, check out branch<br/>file 0600 cred · git clone
  %%> How:
  %%> - Swamp reaches the Node over `@swamp/ssh` from 209
  %%> - `@swamp/cfgmgmt/file` writes the vault token as a 0600 credential file; git reads it, so the token never enters argv
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - clones the repository into the Instance path and checks out the branch
  %%> - removes the credential file at the end of the step
  %%> Returns:
  %%> - the checked-out commit, as this step's output
  %%> Retry:
  %%> - a guard skips the clone when the checkout already exists
  %%> Runs as:
  %%> - the Node's own user, not root
  SW->>N: Prepare the web root<br/>setfacl · @swamp/cfgmgmt/file
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - grants Caddy read access to the web root, and passage through the directories above it
  %%> - denies Caddy the rest of the checkout and its Git directory
  %%> - converges the shared PHP-FPM pool for Instance 42
  %%> How:
  %%> - one `setfacl` per directory as `@swamp/ssh exec` argv (no official ACL behavior)
  %%> - the pool file with `@swamp/cfgmgmt/file`, then a PHP-FPM reload with `@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd`
  %%> - runs beside the next step; both need only the checkout
  %%> Why here:
  %%> - a one-time Instance setup; every Route of Instance 42 then serves without touching the checkout
  %%> Runs as:
  %%> - the Node's managed user; root only above every checkout
  SW->>N: Write .env<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file · 0600
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the rendered `.env` from `vault.get env-5121` into the checkout, owned by the Node user, mode 0600
  %%> - selects the Node's Vite+ store for this Project (`VP_HOME`), so `vp` works in the setup steps
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - renders nothing; the Gateway already rendered `.env`
  %%> - installs no dependencies; `composer install` and `vp install` are setup steps
  %%> - starts no Process; that happens after the setup steps
  SW->>N: Run Project setup steps<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · in order
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - runs the Project's setup steps in order, as the Node's managed user, from the repository root
  %%> Typical steps:
  %%> - `composer install`
  %%> - `vp install`
  %%> - `php artisan migrate`
  %%> How:
  %%> - one `@swamp/ssh exec` per step; the first failure stops the run with that step's exit code
  %%> Limits:
  %%> - each step has its own timeout
  %%> - the whole run stays inside the 60 s budget
  SW->>N: Create, start Processes<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd · forEach
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - creates the Instance's Processes from the Project's Process definitions for `development`
  %%> - starts them, for example the Vite dev server (`vp-dev`) or a queue worker
  %%> How:
  %%> - one `forEach` item per Process, all at once: the unit file and `ensure: running` in `@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd`
  %%> - the behavior's `check` is the end check: each Process is running
  %%> Why here:
  %%> - after the setup steps, because Processes need the installed dependencies
  %%> Today:
  %%> - Project definitions only accept `production`; `development` must be added
  alt all steps pass in budget
    N-->>SW: Processes running<br/>systemd check passed
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the systemd check passed for every Process
    %%> - the checked-out commit is already an output of the clone step
    %%> Not returned:
    %%> - nothing about `.env`; the Gateway rendered and stored it before the run
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · finish-result
  %%> How the Gateway learns it:
  %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the run's outputs
  %%> - Swamp never calls the Gateway; the Gateway reads
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>commit · Instance 42 → active
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the commit is recorded
    %%> - Instance 42 becomes active
    %%> - task #5121 succeeds
  else a step fails or 60 s ends
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or timeout
  %%> When:
  %%> - a step exits with an error, or the 60 s budget runs out
  %%> Effect:
  %%> - the run stops at that step
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed_step, error_code
  %%> The Gateway reads:
  %%> - which step failed
  %%> - its error code
    Note over GW: Keep Instance, mark failed<br/>task → failed · retry is new task
  %%> Result:
  %%> - Instance 42 stays, marked failed, so you can see what happened
  %%> - task #5121 fails
  %%> Retry:
  %%> - a retry is a new task; the Gateway never re-runs work by itself
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5121
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  %%> Returns:
  %%> - the current status
  %%> - the result, once the task has ended
  end
